From: VDR-Suite S1 native SearchTimer versioned revision
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] epgsearch: persist rule revisions and offer v1.1 native snapshot
Upstream-base: 0118b4129c3601c04c7483f2fd04b604d4a2a980
Apply-after: 0001-searchtimer-owner-lock-legacy-writers.patch
Apply-after: 0002-searchtimer-native-generation-observe.patch

For each rule, persist an opaque sr_<32 lowercase hex> revision adjacent to
the immutable native generation in epgsearch.conf comment metadata. Preserve
it across restarts and change it on each successful Save() that sees changed
rule settings, including a change then restore. Only a successfully closed
cSafeFile write marks revised metadata durable. Missing/invalid revisions
remain unauthenticated until a successful Save().

Observe-v1.1 returns the generation, revision and settings under one
epgsearch list lock. The observe-v1.0 ABI remains unchanged.
This adds NO native CAS write capability. Public-v1 mutation endpoints
MUST remain closed until provider guarded writes and readback are verified.
Native build and yaVDR runtime acceptance remain outstanding.

